From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: base: thread: use sched_setaffinity() on Bionic

Bionic does not provide the glibc extension pthread_setaffinity_np(), causing
src/libcamera/base/thread.cpp to fail to compile when targeting Android.

Use pthread_gettid_np() and sched_setaffinity() in
Thread::setThreadAffinityInternal() when building against Bionic (__BIONIC__).

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Android-specific, upstream prefers meson check]
---
diff --git a/src/libcamera/base/thread.cpp b/src/libcamera/base/thread.cpp
index b204355a5..fbb94337e 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/base/thread.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/base/thread.cpp
@@ -462,7 +462,17 @@ void Thread::setThreadAffinityInternal()
 		return;
 
 	const cpu_set_t &cpuset = data_->cpuset_.value();
+#if defined(__BIONIC__)
+	/*
+	 * bionic has no pthread_setaffinity_np(), which is a glibc extension.
+	 * Thread affinity on Linux is a per-tid property anyway, so go through
+	 * the tid and sched_setaffinity() instead.
+	 */
+	sched_setaffinity(pthread_gettid_np(thread_.native_handle()),
+			  sizeof(cpuset), &cpuset);
+#else
 	pthread_setaffinity_np(thread_.native_handle(), sizeof(cpuset), &cpuset);
+#endif
 }
 
